# PM-driven versioning

`info.json` `Version` is `2.{Epic}.{Counter}` from [PM_PLAN.md](../../PM_PLAN.md). Full policy: [docs/Versioning_and_Release_Strategy.md](../../docs/Versioning_and_Release_Strategy.md).

- **Major** locked at **2** (clean-room rewrite).
- **Never go backwards.** UMM is how the player confirms the DLL loaded, so the string must increase on every deploy.
- The **third slot is a strictly increasing counter within the epic**, not the story number. Story progress lives in PM_PLAN only. Start an epic at `2.N.1`; each later ship raises the counter (`2.16.33` → `2.16.35`), whatever story it closes.
- After Epic **6** HUD, leftover work is Epic **7+** (governors **7**, dispatcher **8**, speed/PID **9**, multi-job Maps **10**, catalog **11**, roadside **12**, yard/Prep autonomy **13**, Maps desk **14**, haul/delivery **15**). Do not ship **2.5.x**.
- Bugfix before the next ship → append `.1`, `.2`, … (`2.16.34.10`).
- Docs/rules with no story id → **do not** bump.

Epic 16 is why: `2.16.1` and `2.16.2` matched the story, then the counter ran to `2.16.34.10` while **16.2** was still open. Story **16.3** ships **`2.16.35`** — `2.16.3` would roll UMM backwards.

## When a story is the ship

1. Read PM_PLAN; use **this repo’s** `N.M` ids only.
2. Read the **shipped** `info.json`. The new number must be greater. Never reuse and never lower it.
3. If the story id is unclear, **ask**: “Set `info.json` to `2.N.{next}` and mark **N.M** `[x]`?”
4. If this session is that ship (merge-ready green): set `info.json`, check `[x]`, refresh `docs/PROJECT_STATUS.md` + AGENT_HANDOFF *Current state* in the **same** change. Say the version in the summary.

## Releases

- **Private / smoke:** every story (and sub-patch). Confirm the number in **UMM Version**, not an in-HUD chip.
- **GitHub Release:** every completed **epic**, automatically on epic close (after the close ship is on `main`). Tag `v{info.json Version}`, attach `dist/YardMasterSuite_v*.zip`, player-facing notes. Do not wait to be asked.
- **Nexus Mods:** not until the mod is playable (first player-facing feature). Then help with the page (summary, images, file). Do **not** auto-upload to Nexus.

Local `+BUILD` lives in gitignored `build_number.txt` and the DLL `InformationalVersion` (`2.1.1+104`). Do not commit that file. Do not write `+BUILD` into `info.json`.
